<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African March producer price index up 9.6 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African March producer price index up 9.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 0.1 percent in March from February after rising 0.4 percent in February, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in March was 9.6 percent after February's 9.3 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 0.1 percent month-on-month and 9.7 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Mar'97   Feb'97   Mar'96    - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    9.6	 9.3     5.9	    0.1	0.4</p>
<p>Locally produced   9.5	 9.2     6.6	    0.2	0.4</p>
<p>Imported	    10.1	10.3     3.5	   -0.6	1.0</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Mar'97    Feb'97    Mar'96</p>
<p>All commodities    112.9     112.8     103.0</p>
<p>Locally produced   113.5     113.3     103.7</p>
<p>Imported	     111.1     111.8     100.3</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
